# Single-page app fallback (Netlify).
#
# The site routes on the client: `/` and `/about` are both rendered by
# src/App.jsx, and only `index.html` is ever built. Without this rule a visitor
# who opens or refreshes https://<site>/about asks the host for a file that
# does not exist and gets a 404.
#
# 200 (rather than 301) rewrites rather than redirects, so the URL the visitor
# typed stays in the address bar for the router to read.
/*    /index.html   200
